fuse: let submounts inherit SB_NOSEC from their parent

When the server negotiates FUSE_HANDLE_KILLPRIV_V2 the client marks the
root superblock SB_NOSEC so file_remove_privs() can cache "nothing to
strip" in S_NOSEC and stop issuing a security.capability getxattr before
every write. Submount superblocks (virtiofsd --announce-submounts) are
built by fuse_fill_super_submount(), which starts from fuse_sb_defaults()
and never copies the flag, so writes on a submount pay the getxattr on
every call for the life of the mount. virtiofsd answers each one with an
open/fgetxattr/close of the host file, which on FUSE-backed host
filesystems is a full open-release cycle per write.

Inherit the flag from the parent superblock; it is a property of the
connection, not the mount.

--- a/fs/fuse/inode.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/inode.c
@@ -1595,6 +1595,10 @@ static int fuse_fill_super_submount(struct super_block *sb,
 	struct fuse_inode *fi;
 
 	fuse_sb_defaults(sb);
+	/* KILLPRIV_V2 is negotiated per connection; the parent already
+	 * applied it to its superblock. */
+	if (parent_sb->s_flags & SB_NOSEC)
+		sb->s_flags |= SB_NOSEC;
 	fm->sb = sb;
 
 	WARN_ON(sb->s_bdi != &noop_backing_dev_info);
